WEBVTT

00:00:02.590 --> 00:00:05.650
As of today, we're representatives.

00:00:05.650 --> 00:00:07.900
I never thought we'd make it 
to the Kansai Competition.

00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:09.610
Let's make it to the Nationals.

00:00:09.610 --> 00:00:12.360
Are you not close with those two?

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:15.090
I want to join the club again.

00:01:52.380 --> 00:01:53.380
<b>Music Room</b>

00:01:55.880 --> 00:01:57.080
Okay.

00:01:57.080 --> 00:02:00.970
Please make sure the fortissimo 
at L doesn't sound muddy.

00:02:00.970 --> 00:02:01.800
Okay.

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:05.390
Don't be sloppy on the snare roll.

00:02:05.390 --> 00:02:06.480
Okay!

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:09.810
That's it for today's rehearsal.

00:02:10.460 --> 00:02:12.900
We'll be entering the Bon holiday 
starting tomorrow,

00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:14.940
but we'll be going to camp right after.

00:02:15.430 --> 00:02:18.050
Take care of your health.

00:02:18.050 --> 00:02:20.110
Please try not to catch a cold.

00:02:20.110 --> 00:02:20.740
Okay!

00:02:23.060 --> 00:02:24.940
Please try.

00:02:25.660 --> 00:02:26.580
Okay...

00:02:26.580 --> 00:02:29.530
Okay, I'm going to go over 
the camp itinerary.

00:02:29.530 --> 00:02:32.830
Section leaders, please gather 
at the usual classroom.

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:40.240
Kumiko-chan!

00:02:41.450 --> 00:02:45.210
Are you going anywhere for the Bon break?

00:02:45.210 --> 00:02:47.520
No, not really.

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:48.730
Really?

00:02:49.090 --> 00:02:52.230
Then let's go to the pool!

00:02:52.620 --> 00:02:53.770
Pool?

00:02:54.060 --> 00:02:54.860
Pool?

00:02:54.860 --> 00:02:58.610
I was wondering if you wanted 
to come with us to the pool.

00:02:58.610 --> 00:02:59.550
I'll go.

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:02.320
What?

00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:05.240
No, I just wasn't expecting that.

00:03:05.240 --> 00:03:08.540
The swimsuit I bought last year 
is getting pretty tight.

00:03:09.130 --> 00:03:11.410
I want to wear it at least this once.

00:03:12.450 --> 00:03:13.670
<i>Tight?</i>

00:03:13.670 --> 00:03:15.000
<i>You mean...</i>

00:03:18.740 --> 00:03:23.640
<i>So it is true that your breasts grow 
when you enter high school.</i>

00:03:24.990 --> 00:03:28.640
<i>Episode 2 
Hesitation Flute</i>

00:03:28.880 --> 00:03:31.140
Whoa, it's bustling!

00:03:31.510 --> 00:03:33.650
It's Bon break, after all.

00:03:33.650 --> 00:03:35.900
Sweet, let's swim!

00:03:38.790 --> 00:03:40.240
Hey!

00:03:40.630 --> 00:03:43.310
Hazuki-chan's a good swimmer.

00:03:43.310 --> 00:03:44.320
I'm here.

00:03:46.940 --> 00:03:49.780
I worked up the courage 
to buy this last year.

00:03:50.240 --> 00:03:52.040
But it was a bit too grown-up, so...

00:03:52.040 --> 00:03:54.800
No, it looks really good on you.

00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:56.170
Does it?

00:03:56.790 --> 00:03:59.170
I'm going to go buy some drinks.

00:03:59.170 --> 00:04:01.330
I saved a spot over there.

00:04:01.710 --> 00:04:02.950
Thanks.

00:04:04.050 --> 00:04:08.620
<i>I hope I'm big enough next year 
for a swimsuit like that one.</i>

00:04:09.710 --> 00:04:10.740
Oh, hey.

00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:13.540
Oh, Kaori-senpai.

00:04:13.540 --> 00:04:15.500
You guys are here, too, huh?

00:04:15.500 --> 00:04:16.560
Just you two?

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:19.010
Hazuki-chan and Midori-chan are with us.

00:04:19.010 --> 00:04:19.900
Senpai—

00:04:23.350 --> 00:04:24.980
Wh-Who are you?

00:04:26.480 --> 00:04:28.320
You're so mean.

00:04:28.320 --> 00:04:30.450
We're with each other all the time.

00:04:31.370 --> 00:04:32.920
Asuka-senpai?

00:04:32.920 --> 00:04:35.040
What are you doing here?

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:38.200
It's not like I don't ever come to the pool.

00:04:38.200 --> 00:04:40.840
Today's about the only break we have.

00:04:40.840 --> 00:04:42.840
The others are here, too.

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:45.260
Oh, my god! Oh, my god! Oh, my god!

00:04:44.320 --> 00:04:45.260
Wait, Yuko...

00:04:45.260 --> 00:04:47.290
Holy smokes, Kaori-senpai!

00:04:47.290 --> 00:04:49.270
You're like an angel from the heavens!

00:04:49.270 --> 00:04:51.520
What's up with the sad T-shirt?

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:53.100
What, got a problem?

00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:57.960
You're one to talk, with a shirt 
that says "cement addiction" on it.

00:04:59.940 --> 00:05:04.190
Meanwhile, yours says,
 "My staple food is love."

00:05:04.190 --> 00:05:06.720
Who cares about the English?

00:05:06.720 --> 00:05:07.740
We're in Japan.

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:09.620
You started it.

00:05:10.740 --> 00:05:12.840
Midori-chan.

00:05:14.260 --> 00:05:15.720
What's up?

00:05:15.720 --> 00:05:17.420
We're here to buy ice cream.

00:05:17.420 --> 00:05:19.690
That's actually just an excuse.

00:05:19.690 --> 00:05:22.380
We're actually here to get away 
from the senpais.

00:05:22.380 --> 00:05:25.130
Huh? Are they here, too?

00:05:25.130 --> 00:05:26.140
Yeah.

00:05:26.140 --> 00:05:30.500
Natsuki-senpai and Yuko-senpai 
are at it again, and man...

00:05:31.850 --> 00:05:33.340
Kumiko, ice cream?

00:05:33.340 --> 00:05:34.930
Oh, right.

00:05:37.810 --> 00:05:39.710
What's wrong, Kumiko?

00:05:39.710 --> 00:05:42.070
Sorry, I have to do something.

00:05:42.070 --> 00:05:43.330
What about ice cream?

00:05:43.330 --> 00:05:44.480
Yes, please.

00:05:45.640 --> 00:05:47.220
Nozomi-senpai!

00:05:47.890 --> 00:05:50.040
Oh. You're...

00:05:50.040 --> 00:05:52.010
Aren't you the euphonium?

00:05:53.030 --> 00:05:54.780
Kumiko Oumae-chan.

00:05:54.780 --> 00:05:55.850
Yes.

00:05:55.850 --> 00:05:57.320
Natsuki's here, too.

00:05:57.320 --> 00:05:58.580
We came here together.

00:05:58.580 --> 00:06:00.500
Oh, I saw her earlier.

00:06:00.500 --> 00:06:02.590
Asuka-senpai, too.

00:06:02.590 --> 00:06:03.820
No way.

00:06:07.530 --> 00:06:09.470
I think I'll lay off for today.

00:06:11.680 --> 00:06:15.580
Oh, yeah. You're in the 
competition team, aren't you?

00:06:15.580 --> 00:06:16.560
Yes.

00:06:16.560 --> 00:06:18.730
Natsuki the second-year is support crew,

00:06:18.730 --> 00:06:21.740
and you, the first-year, 
are in the competition team.

00:06:23.300 --> 00:06:24.820
What's up with that?

00:06:31.370 --> 00:06:32.370
<b>Go for the gold!
 We'll play together next year!</b>

00:06:37.250 --> 00:06:40.210
I... I don't think it can be helped.

00:06:40.850 --> 00:06:43.260
So long as Kitauji is 
aiming for the Nationals,

00:06:43.260 --> 00:06:44.970
it's only natural that the better player

00:06:44.970 --> 00:06:47.670
has to play, no matter what grade they're in.

00:06:50.120 --> 00:06:52.140
Yeah, I think so, too.

00:06:53.680 --> 00:06:56.270
Kitauji sure has changed.

00:06:57.280 --> 00:06:58.380
See you.

00:06:58.380 --> 00:06:59.100
Hey.

00:06:59.710 --> 00:07:02.060
Why Asuka-senpai?

00:07:03.190 --> 00:07:05.210
Why don't you talk to the president

00:07:05.210 --> 00:07:07.660
or to the teacher if you want 
to come back to the club?

00:07:09.190 --> 00:07:12.160
Asuka-senpai is special.

00:07:12.160 --> 00:07:13.490
Special?

00:07:13.490 --> 00:07:15.450
Does it make you curious?

00:07:15.450 --> 00:07:17.040
It does.

00:07:18.470 --> 00:07:19.500
Okay.

00:07:23.610 --> 00:07:27.060
Asuka-senpai stopped me.

00:07:27.730 --> 00:07:30.630
When I got in a fight with the third-years,

00:07:30.630 --> 00:07:33.180
and quit along with the other kids...

00:07:32.180 --> 00:07:33.180
<b>Resignation</b>

00:07:33.180 --> 00:07:34.180
<b>Staff Room</b>

00:07:34.460 --> 00:07:35.980
Pardon me.

00:07:36.680 --> 00:07:38.560
So you're really quitting.

00:07:40.100 --> 00:07:41.480
That's stupid.

00:07:42.060 --> 00:07:43.850
There's no point being in a club

00:07:43.850 --> 00:07:47.030
where the serious people 
get shoved around by losers.

00:07:47.030 --> 00:07:49.410
That's what I mean!

00:07:49.410 --> 00:07:51.170
That's stupid.

00:07:51.840 --> 00:07:58.200
Just ignore those loser third-years, 
and it'll just be us next year.

00:07:58.200 --> 00:08:00.250
Can't you wait until then?

00:08:00.830 --> 00:08:01.910
I can't.

00:08:01.910 --> 00:08:03.140
Oh.

00:08:05.700 --> 00:08:12.020
Come to think of it now, Asuka-senpai 
was trying to get me to stay.

00:08:12.020 --> 00:08:13.500
So that's why.

00:08:14.180 --> 00:08:17.050
It's Asuka-senpai's last year.

00:08:17.050 --> 00:08:19.400
So I wanted to do something to help.

00:08:20.780 --> 00:08:23.100
I don't mind if we can't perform together.

00:08:23.670 --> 00:08:25.690
I just want to be useful.

00:08:26.150 --> 00:08:29.730
Does Asuka-senpai know about that?

00:08:30.150 --> 00:08:31.160
Yeah.

00:08:31.660 --> 00:08:33.900
Then I wonder why.

00:08:34.510 --> 00:08:37.120
I don't know. That's why it sucks.

00:08:39.000 --> 00:08:43.200
Kaori-senpai was such 
an angel in her swimsuit.

00:08:43.200 --> 00:08:44.380
Oh, cool.

00:08:44.820 --> 00:08:46.350
My friend's coming.

00:08:46.350 --> 00:08:47.480
Move.

00:08:47.480 --> 00:08:48.780
Your friend?

00:08:48.780 --> 00:08:50.560
You have friends?

00:08:50.560 --> 00:08:52.650
Unlike you.

00:08:52.650 --> 00:08:55.400
So who's the kind soul?

00:08:56.120 --> 00:08:58.280
Shut up already.

00:08:58.280 --> 00:08:59.470
It's Nozomi.

00:09:00.140 --> 00:09:01.680
Nozomi Kasaki.

00:09:02.490 --> 00:09:03.810
Nozomi...

00:09:05.250 --> 00:09:06.810
Yuko and Mizore?

00:09:06.810 --> 00:09:07.940
Yes.

00:09:07.940 --> 00:09:12.380
They're both from the Minami Middle School 
concert band like you, right?

00:09:12.380 --> 00:09:13.580
Yeah.

00:09:13.580 --> 00:09:17.440
I was wondering why those two didn't quit.

00:09:18.150 --> 00:09:20.950
I tried talking to Yuko about it,

00:09:20.950 --> 00:09:22.840
but she said she'd hold out 
for a little longer.

00:09:22.840 --> 00:09:24.500
And Yoroizuka-senpai?

00:09:24.500 --> 00:09:25.870
Mizore...

00:09:28.740 --> 00:09:30.810
I didn't talk to her.

00:09:31.250 --> 00:09:32.670
Why not?

00:09:33.070 --> 00:09:35.810
She was the only oboe.

00:09:35.810 --> 00:09:39.140
And none of the senpais pestered her.

00:09:39.880 --> 00:09:44.350
Besides, she was a competition 
member from the beginning.

00:09:47.350 --> 00:09:48.810
I see.

00:09:50.720 --> 00:09:52.820
Why do you even ask?

00:09:53.500 --> 00:09:57.060
I thought maybe I could 
figure out why Asuka-senpai

00:09:57.060 --> 00:09:58.820
doesn't accept you rejoining.

00:09:59.560 --> 00:10:00.370
Did you?

00:10:00.740 --> 00:10:02.790
No.

00:10:02.790 --> 00:10:04.080
Of course.

00:10:07.270 --> 00:10:08.370
Um...

00:10:08.920 --> 00:10:09.790
Yeah?

00:10:09.790 --> 00:10:13.920
Why did you decide to join 
the band again, Nozomi-senpai?

00:10:16.810 --> 00:10:18.190
I guess it's weird.

00:10:18.190 --> 00:10:19.130
No.

00:10:19.650 --> 00:10:23.100
It's not exactly weird.

00:10:23.940 --> 00:10:27.180
I like concert band.

00:10:28.290 --> 00:10:33.320
I wanted to practice hard so we could 
compete against the best schools.

00:10:33.320 --> 00:10:36.160
But everyone was afraid of the senpais.

00:10:36.700 --> 00:10:41.170
I tried to do something, 
but I just got ignored.

00:10:41.600 --> 00:10:47.120
It seemed like there was no more 
hope, so I gave up and quit.

00:10:48.170 --> 00:10:51.330
And now, this year, 
we're in the Kansai Competition.

00:10:51.330 --> 00:10:53.090
Honestly, I can't believe it.

00:10:53.740 --> 00:10:56.050
It's like I was being a complete idiot.

00:10:56.600 --> 00:10:57.950
Don't you think?

00:10:58.520 --> 00:11:00.380
I don't think so.

00:11:00.930 --> 00:11:06.810
Asuka-senpai told me I wouldn't add 
anything to the club if I rejoined.

00:11:08.280 --> 00:11:11.600
I told her I'd work on any of my faults.

00:11:13.010 --> 00:11:14.020
Why?

00:11:14.780 --> 00:11:16.860
What am I doing wrong?

00:11:17.570 --> 00:11:20.070
I don't get it.

00:11:21.750 --> 00:11:23.030
I'm sorry.

00:11:24.350 --> 00:11:25.350
Don't worry.

00:11:25.350 --> 00:11:26.670
I'm okay.

00:11:26.670 --> 00:11:27.880
See you.

00:11:27.880 --> 00:11:29.010
Thanks.

00:11:30.600 --> 00:11:32.620
So stop coming by.

00:11:35.580 --> 00:11:38.050
Senpai, I'll ask her.

00:11:38.460 --> 00:11:42.280
I'll ask why you can't join.

00:11:43.040 --> 00:11:45.530
I'll ask Asuka-senpai.

00:11:46.250 --> 00:11:47.630
Thanks.

00:11:48.260 --> 00:11:49.940
But it's okay.

00:11:49.940 --> 00:11:51.850
Thanks for the gesture, though.

00:11:52.160 --> 00:11:53.650
No...

00:11:54.040 --> 00:11:56.630
By the way, don't you have to go?

00:11:56.630 --> 00:11:58.220
Aren't your friends waiting?

00:12:01.030 --> 00:12:03.840
Kumiko-chan's late.

00:12:04.270 --> 00:12:05.170
Yeah.

00:12:05.170 --> 00:12:05.950
Go!

00:12:17.430 --> 00:12:23.220
<i>The Bon holiday was over before we knew it, 
and our three-day camp began.</i>

00:12:25.040 --> 00:12:26.600
It's big.

00:12:26.600 --> 00:12:29.520
I bet we'll get a lot of practice done here.

00:12:30.010 --> 00:12:31.380
Good morning.

00:12:31.560 --> 00:12:33.030
Good morning.

00:12:33.030 --> 00:12:34.860
You're here already?

00:12:34.860 --> 00:12:35.950
Yes.

00:12:35.950 --> 00:12:40.820
I didn't want to make Michie-sensei 
run everything by herself.

00:12:40.820 --> 00:12:44.870
But you're always there 
early for rehearsals, too.

00:12:44.870 --> 00:12:47.710
My job is rewarding. It's worth the effort.

00:12:47.710 --> 00:12:48.540
Yes.

00:12:48.950 --> 00:12:49.910
Besides...

00:12:52.650 --> 00:12:55.920
...I don't have a wife or kids.

00:12:55.920 --> 00:12:58.880
I don't really have anything 
to do besides work.

00:13:04.760 --> 00:13:06.720
I'll ask her.

00:13:10.880 --> 00:13:11.770
What?

00:13:11.770 --> 00:13:12.640
Oh, nothing.

00:13:13.920 --> 00:13:17.460
<i>Why did I say that?</i>

00:13:21.780 --> 00:13:27.600
Now, before we begin practice, 
there's someone I'd like to introduce.

00:13:27.600 --> 00:13:28.320
Come in.

00:13:39.480 --> 00:13:42.280
This is Satomi Niiyama-sensei.

00:13:42.280 --> 00:13:44.380
Starting today, she's going 
to instruct the woodwinds.

00:13:44.800 --> 00:13:47.040
My name is Satomi Niiyama.

00:13:47.040 --> 00:13:48.290
Nice to meet you.

00:13:50.310 --> 00:13:51.170
Woodwinds?

00:13:51.170 --> 00:13:52.090
Yes!

00:13:52.090 --> 00:13:53.500
She's gorgeous.

00:13:53.500 --> 00:13:55.140
Good job, Taki-sensei.

00:13:55.140 --> 00:13:56.520
What, really?

00:13:56.520 --> 00:13:59.220
The woodwinds will be in the 
Second Hall for the afternoon.

00:13:59.220 --> 00:14:02.230
Percussion and brass will practice here.

00:14:02.920 --> 00:14:06.160
Niiyama-sensei may be young, 
but she's very talented.

00:14:06.160 --> 00:14:08.470
Be sure to follow her instruction well.

00:14:08.470 --> 00:14:10.120
"Very talented"?

00:14:10.120 --> 00:14:11.870
Flattery will get you nowhere.

00:14:11.870 --> 00:14:15.330
No, I'm only telling the truth.

00:14:15.330 --> 00:14:16.830
My.

00:14:16.830 --> 00:14:20.000
I'm honored that you would 
say that of me, Taki-sensei.

00:14:20.000 --> 00:14:21.130
What was that?

00:14:21.130 --> 00:14:21.960
Is it serious?

00:14:21.960 --> 00:14:23.000
Think it's serious?

00:14:26.130 --> 00:14:31.010
<i>Sitting there was Reina, 
with the eyes of a dead fish.</i>

00:14:32.510 --> 00:14:35.600
Yay. I love curry.

00:14:36.090 --> 00:14:38.310
Good work on the sectionals.

00:14:38.310 --> 00:14:42.560
I feel left out being with the woodwinds, 
even though I'm a contrabass.

00:14:42.840 --> 00:14:45.690
So how is Niiyama-sensei?

00:14:45.690 --> 00:14:47.220
You know what?

00:14:47.220 --> 00:14:49.700
She was as incredible as Taki-sensei.

00:14:53.460 --> 00:14:55.580
Let's try that again!

00:14:55.580 --> 00:14:58.020
Dozens of times.

00:14:58.020 --> 00:15:00.030
That sounds rough, too.

00:15:00.030 --> 00:15:02.880
That does sound like Taki-sensei, though.

00:15:02.880 --> 00:15:04.970
What about you guys, Hazuki-chan?

00:15:04.970 --> 00:15:06.420
It's brutal.

00:15:06.420 --> 00:15:10.950
She's, like, "I hope you kids understand."

00:15:12.140 --> 00:15:13.930
Thank you for the meal.

00:15:19.540 --> 00:15:22.230
<i>Anything I say might only make things worse.</i>

00:15:24.760 --> 00:15:25.720
Yeah.

00:15:26.190 --> 00:15:27.360
Yeah.

00:15:27.970 --> 00:15:29.390
I'm not sure.

00:15:31.270 --> 00:15:31.910
Yeah.

00:15:33.660 --> 00:15:35.420
Okay, bye.

00:15:38.870 --> 00:15:41.190
I heard you talked to Nozomi at the pool.

00:15:41.610 --> 00:15:42.420
Yes.

00:15:43.210 --> 00:15:45.450
She said thanks.

00:15:45.450 --> 00:15:49.520
And she said you don't 
need to do so much for her.

00:15:49.520 --> 00:15:50.860
But...

00:15:50.860 --> 00:15:52.580
She doesn't want to

00:15:52.580 --> 00:15:55.980
cause trouble for her underclassmen, 
especially after what happened last year.

00:15:58.190 --> 00:16:01.650
You must really like Nozomi-senpai.

00:16:01.650 --> 00:16:03.380
More like...

00:16:04.360 --> 00:16:05.770
...I look up to her, I guess.

00:16:07.530 --> 00:16:10.840
Nozomi was the president of the 
Minami Middle School concert band.

00:16:10.840 --> 00:16:13.870
She was the exact opposite of me, 
in that she had patience

00:16:13.870 --> 00:16:15.240
for complicated things.

00:16:18.870 --> 00:16:19.620
<b>Music Room</b>

00:16:23.530 --> 00:16:26.340
But Nozomi is honest to a fault.

00:16:26.720 --> 00:16:29.420
She got in a fight with 
the third-years last year.

00:16:29.800 --> 00:16:32.970
Please, I want to practice 
for the competition.

00:16:32.970 --> 00:16:34.130
Please.

00:16:34.690 --> 00:16:38.880
Not only did I not help her, 
I only made things worse.

00:16:39.640 --> 00:16:41.490
Don't bother.

00:16:42.210 --> 00:16:44.520
Those kids are total divas.

00:16:44.520 --> 00:16:46.070
You said that?

00:16:46.070 --> 00:16:47.730
To the third-years?

00:16:47.730 --> 00:16:49.740
I was in the moment.

00:16:52.290 --> 00:16:54.960
So I guess I'm trying to make up for it

00:16:55.600 --> 00:16:57.740
by helping her get back into the club.

00:16:58.300 --> 00:17:03.110
I couldn't do anything for her 
when she was really suffering.

00:17:05.630 --> 00:17:07.750
Sorry to worry you.

00:17:08.110 --> 00:17:11.480
But you have to focus on the 
Kansai Competition, Oumae-chan.

00:17:11.480 --> 00:17:14.040
I'll take care of Nozomi.

00:17:15.400 --> 00:17:19.390
<i>"Okay." It should have
been easy to just say that,</i>

00:17:19.390 --> 00:17:23.450
<i>but the word got caught in my throat.</i>

00:17:49.710 --> 00:17:56.070
Asuka-senpai told me I wouldn't add 
anything to the club if I rejoined.

00:17:56.540 --> 00:17:59.030
So I guess I'm trying to make up for it

00:17:59.720 --> 00:18:01.850
by helping her get back into the club.

00:18:01.850 --> 00:18:06.440
<i>Why doesn't Asuka-senpai want 
Nozomi-senpai back in the club?</i>

00:18:06.740 --> 00:18:12.180
If she lets her in and she thrashes around, 
it would affect the Kansai Competition.

00:18:12.180 --> 00:18:15.080
I think Asuka-senpai is 
making the right decision.

00:18:15.080 --> 00:18:17.630
<i>Maybe that's true, but...</i>

00:18:19.270 --> 00:18:23.740
To be honest, I genuinely don't care.

00:18:24.210 --> 00:18:27.330
I don't give a damn 
who plays a solo or whatever.

00:18:28.230 --> 00:18:31.630
I wish summer would go on forever.

00:18:32.290 --> 00:18:35.250
<i>What is she actually thinking?</i>

00:18:41.580 --> 00:18:43.230
Yoroizuka-senpai!

00:18:43.820 --> 00:18:45.610
Please turn that piece off.

00:18:45.610 --> 00:18:46.430
I hate it.

00:18:46.430 --> 00:18:48.440
Sorry.

00:18:49.290 --> 00:18:51.800
Senpai, why are you here?

00:18:51.800 --> 00:18:53.540
Rhythm games.

00:18:54.240 --> 00:18:55.640
I can't sleep.

00:18:57.400 --> 00:18:58.650
Come sit.

00:18:58.650 --> 00:18:59.990
Right.

00:18:59.990 --> 00:19:03.490
You can play rhythm games without the audio?

00:19:07.110 --> 00:19:09.960
Hey, do you like competitions?

00:19:09.960 --> 00:19:11.040
Huh?

00:19:11.410 --> 00:19:12.910
I hate them.

00:19:12.910 --> 00:19:15.820
They end up depending on the judges' tastes.

00:19:18.240 --> 00:19:25.060
But I kind of think that's 
just how it has to be.

00:19:26.950 --> 00:19:28.560
How it has to be?

00:19:28.560 --> 00:19:31.510
Even though it makes 
a lot of people miserable?

00:19:33.120 --> 00:19:34.730
Sorry.

00:19:36.470 --> 00:19:38.320
I'm hurting.

00:19:39.290 --> 00:19:41.700
I wish competitions didn't exist.

00:19:47.680 --> 00:19:52.830
Then, like, why are you continuing with band?

00:19:54.250 --> 00:19:55.500
<b>Silver    Minami Public Middle School</b>

00:19:54.840 --> 00:19:57.850
Let's promise to get first place 
when we're in high school.

00:20:00.400 --> 00:20:02.090
I don't know.

00:20:04.020 --> 00:20:05.010
Senpai?

00:20:05.010 --> 00:20:06.010
<b>Paused</b>

00:20:05.010 --> 00:20:06.010
<b>Would You Like To...

00:20:10.770 --> 00:20:12.060
<b>Gold    Kitauji High School</b>

00:20:14.500 --> 00:20:18.070
I really don't know anymore.

00:20:35.670 --> 00:20:37.480
Where were you?

00:20:37.480 --> 00:20:39.280
I couldn't sleep.

00:20:39.850 --> 00:20:40.780
Oh.

00:20:48.360 --> 00:20:49.360
Yeah?

00:20:49.680 --> 00:20:53.710
Do you think Taki-sensei 
is going out with Niiyama-sensei?

00:20:53.710 --> 00:20:56.810
He probably prefers someone 
closer to his own age, right?

00:20:58.430 --> 00:21:00.280
There's no way to know.

00:21:00.280 --> 00:21:02.750
You have to ask him directly.

00:21:04.660 --> 00:21:05.740
You think so?

00:21:05.740 --> 00:21:06.910
Yeah.

00:21:07.670 --> 00:21:09.700
Don't worry, Reina.

00:21:09.700 --> 00:21:11.780
You seem grown-up.

00:21:11.780 --> 00:21:13.240
What do you mean by that?

00:21:13.240 --> 00:21:14.920
I'm serious.

00:21:14.920 --> 00:21:18.280
We're the same age, 
but you seem totally different.

00:21:18.280 --> 00:21:19.880
Both inside and outside.

00:21:52.380 --> 00:21:53.860
Asuka-senpai.

00:21:54.840 --> 00:21:57.220
Do you have some time later?

00:21:58.030 --> 00:22:00.300
There's something I want 
to talk to you about.

00:22:03.810 --> 00:22:07.310
<i>And the next piece begins.</i>
